# Mid-trace ISR_SYNC barrier.
#
# Phase 1: some independent per-channel work on ch=0 and ch=1.
# Phase 2: ISR_SYNC (drains all channels via a 32-way blocking barrier).
# Phase 3: more work on ch=0 and ch=1 (must wait for SYNC to complete).
# Phase 4: ISR_EOC (frontend's "trace done" hook).
#
# Validates that:
#   - ISR_SYNC's per-channel blocking aim_reqs all complete
#   - the dispatcher resumes after SYNC clears all stalls
#   - phase-3 work runs to completion
#   - ISR_EOC still fires its frontend callback at the end

# Phase 1
AiM WR_BIAS 4 0x00000001
AiM MAC_ABK 63 0x00000001 0
AiM RD_MAC 4 0x00000001
AiM WR_BIAS 4 0x00000002
AiM MAC_ABK 63 0x00000002 0
AiM RD_MAC 4 0x00000002

# Phase 2: barrier
AiM ISR_SYNC

# Phase 3
AiM WR_BIAS 4 0x00000001
AiM MAC_ABK 63 0x00000001 1
AiM RD_MAC 4 0x00000001
AiM WR_BIAS 4 0x00000002
AiM MAC_ABK 63 0x00000002 1
AiM RD_MAC 4 0x00000002

# Phase 4
AiM ISR_EOC
